# Where the lead agent and the dev server may connect, and nothing else.
#
# One line per host: the name, the ports it is allowed on, and why, after a
# `#`. A line without a reason is refused, so the machine boots no lead.
# `lead-egress.ts apply` reads this file as root at boot and every 10 minutes,
# resolves each name, allows exactly those addresses on those ports for the
# `lead` and `cwdev` users, and pins the names in /etc/hosts. Those users'
# DNS is refused, so a name that is not here does not resolve for them.
# Loopback is always allowed; the board server refuses both users' loopback
# TCP calls, and the lead reaches its board through its socket.
#
# Changing this file is an image deploy (machine:deploy).

api.anthropic.com   tcp/443  # Claude Code's model API, flags and the WebFetch safety check (Anthropic's network-config page: required)
platform.claude.com tcp/443  # OAuth token exchange and refresh for the lead's sign-in (network-config page: required for every sign-in)
claude.ai           tcp/443  # claude.ai account authentication; assumed needed for Remote Control (CW_LEAD_REMOTE_CONTROL), unchecked
github.com          tcp/22   # git fetch of the project repo over SSH with the read-only deploy key (lead.sh); pushes go through the server
